    "body": "Adds docs/demo.html, a self-contained page that renders through the full pipeline using only CSS properties HoneyBee supports today.\n\n## Why\n\nUntil now, the only page we've loaded in the browser is the hardcoded welcome string in window.cpp, which uses single-value px properties and hex colors -- the simplest possible subset. It exercises parse -> cascade -> layout -> paint, but not shorthand expansion, not em/auto resolution, not class selectors, not background-color.\n\nThe demo page exercises all of those. It becomes:\n- The reproducible visual smoke test for v0.1.0\n- The asset for a screenshot in release notes and docs/current-state.md\n- A page future ADRs can extend as new properties land\n\n## What it exercises\n\n- body { background-color } -- whole-page background\n- .card { width: 520px; margin: 20px auto; padding: 24px;\n          background-color: #fff; border-width: 2px; border-color: #999 }\n- h1 { font-size: 32px; color: #d35400 }\n- .highlight { background-color: #fff3cd; color: #856404; padding: 12px }\n- Arabic text with correct shaping via Pango\n\n## What it deliberately does not use\n\nOnly properties the current pipeline supports. Deliberately excluded, because they would render as nothing:\n- border-radius, box-shadow (not implemented)\n- font shorthand (not implemented; would be silently dropped)\n- max-width (not implemented)\n- text-align (not implemented)\n- background shorthand (only background-color is supported)\n- light-dark(), vh units\n\nEach of those is a documented gap in docs/current-state.md (upcoming PR). The demo stays honest by not using them.\n\n## Verification\n\nRan ./build/bin/honeybee, loaded http://127.0.0.1:8000/demo.html via a local HTTP server, saw the expected render:\n\n- Gray page background\n- White card, centered horizontally, 2px gray border\n- 24px padding inside the card\n- Orange 32px heading\n- Yellow-highlighted paragraph\n- Connected Arabic text\n\nNo code changes. No CMake changes. Test suite untouched.\n\n## After merge\n\nThe docs PR (feature matrix, ADR index, current-state page, CONTRIBUTING gotchas) will reference this page and include its screenshot. Then tag v0.1.0.\n",
